/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A roller chain is a set of short links.
   - Types: roller chain (bush roller chain) for power transmission; silent or inverted-tooth chain, where shaped plates engage the sprocket teeth and there are no rollers, used at high speed and low noise; block chain, simple cast blocks for lo
   - The standard number fixes the pitch p (distance between pin centres), the roller diameter and the inner width.
   - Let Z₁ be the teeth on the small sprocket, Z₂ on the large, p the pitch and N₁ the small-sprocket speed in rev/min.
   - v is the mean chain speed in m/s; Z₁ is the teeth on the small sprocket; p is the pitch in m; N₁ is its speed in rev/min.
   - The pitch diameter is the circle through the roller centres, not the tip circle.
   - d is the pitch diameter; p is the pitch; Z is the number of teeth.
   - Chordal action: the chain wraps the sprocket as a polygon, so the link speed rises and falls between πdN/60 and πdN/60 × cos(180°/Z).
   - Chain length is counted in pitches (links).
   - L is the chain length in pitches; C is the centre distance; p is the pitch.
*/
