/* book Worked example: Q: A 3 kW, 1000 rpm electric motor drives a compressor at 500 rpm through a single-strand 08B roller chain (p = 12.7 mm, breaking load 17.8 kN). Z₁ = 19, Z₂ = 38 and the centre distance is about 500 mm. The service factor is 1.3, and the maker’s chart rates one strand of 08B at 4.5 kW at 1000 rpm on a 19-tooth sprocket. Check the chain, and find the pitch diameters, the chain speed, the chain pull, the factor of safety, the number of links with the exact centre distance, and the speed variation. Neglect centrifugal tension and sag.
   1. Speed ratio: Z₂/Z₁ = 38/19 = 2, so the compressor turns at 1000/2 = 500 rpm.
   2. Design power: 1.3 × 3 = 3.9 kW. The 08B rating of 4.5 kW is above it, so a single strand of 08B is acceptable.
   3. Pitch diameters: d₁ = 12.7/sin(180°/19) = 12.7/sin 9.474° = 12.7/0.1646 = 77.16 mm; d₂ = 12.7/sin 4.737° = 12.7/0.08258 = 153.79 mm.
   4. Mean chain speed: v = Z₁pN₁/60 = 19 × 0.0127 × 1000/60 = 4.022 m/s.
   5. Chain pull: F = P/v = 3000/4.022 = 746 N.
   6. Factor of safety on breaking load: 17 800/746 = 23.9. The chain is far from breaking; the power rating, which allows for plate fatigue and wear, is the real limit.
   7. Length: 2C/p = 1000/12.7 = 78.74; (Z₁ + Z₂)/2 = 28.5; ((Z₂ − Z₁)/(2π))² = (19/6.283)² = 3.024² = 9.144, and 9.144 × 12.7/500 = 0.23. L = 78.74 + 28.5 + 0.23 = 107.47 pitches.
   8. Round up to an even number: 108 links. Exact centre distance: A = 108 − 28.5 = 79.5, 8B² = 8 × 9.144 = 73.15, so C = (12.7/4)[79.5 + √(6320.25 − 73.15)] = 3.175 × (79.5 + 79.04) = 503.4 mm.
   9. Speed variation: 1 − cos 9.474° = 1 − 0.98636 = 0.0136, or 1.36 %. The link speed swings between π × 0.07716 × 1000/60 = 4.040 m/s and 4.040 × 0.98636 = 3.985 m/s.
   Answer: One strand of 08B is enough (3.9 kW design power against a 4.5 kW rating). d₁ = 77.16 mm, d₂ = 153.79 mm, v = 4.02 m/s, F = 746 N, factor of safety 23.9, 108 links at a centre distance of 503.4 mm, and a speed variation of 1.36 %. */
