/* book exam traps: Rounding to an odd number of links. An odd count needs a weaker offset link; round up to even and recompute C: 108 links put the sprockets 503.4 mm apart, not 500 mm. | Using the tip diameter instead of the pitch diameter d = p/sin(180°/Z). The chain sits on the pitch circle. | Choosing a chain from the motor power alone. Compare the rating with the design power: 3.9 kW, not 3 kW, in the worked example. | Writing the speed variation as cos(180°/Z) instead of 1 − cos(180°/Z): 1.36 %, not 98.6 %, at 19 teeth. | Setting a chain as tight as a V-belt. It needs a little slack; too tight overloads the shaft bearings. */
