/* book: lead: A wire rope is a bundle of steel wires twisted into strands and then into a rope. It carries load only in tension: every wire shares the pull, so the rope is strong yet bends round a sheave. Cranes, lifts, mine hoists and bridge stays use it where a chain would be too heavy or a belt would slip. Selection fixes the construction and lay, sizes the diameter from the breaking load, and then checks th */
